{"chunk_id": "2b86be6efc11", "text": "Vyasa urges Yudhishthira to begin the Ashvamedha (Horse\u2011sacrifice), assuring him that the immense gifts of gold and the proper performance of the rite will cleanse the sin of killing his kinsmen in the war. The king undertakes the ritual with exact adherence to Vedic prescriptions. Priests conduct complex ceremonies\u2014Pravargya, Soma rites, and the preparation of numerous sacrificial stakes\u2014while Bhima distributes endless food so that no visitor is poor or hungry. Animals, including the wandering sacrificial horse, are consecrated and offered. Draupadi participates in the culminating rite, and Yudhishthira symbolically inhales the purifying smoke. When the sacrifice ends, the king gives vast wealth to the Brahmanas and even donates the entire Earth to Vyasa, declaring his willingness to renounce it, astonishing the assembly.\nYudhishthira completes the Ashvamedha sacrifice, ritually offers the horse, distributes immense gifts, and even symbolically gives the Earth to the Brahmanas.\nThemes: Ashvamedha sacrifice, ritual purification, royal generosity, atonement for war, Vedic ritual authority", "vector": [-0.0037934028077870607, -0.014083133079111576, -0.0016639773966744542, 0.002722871955484152, -0.01864452473819256, 0.029176954180002213, -0.039150845259428024, -0.011403481476008892, -0.0043552652932703495, -0.00750701455399394, 0.0017570670461282134, 0.015838537365198135, 0.004016153048723936, -0.001062219263985753, -0.01962861604988575, 0.01903018169105053, 0.04941730201244354, -0.0015501087764278054, 0.01775352470576763, 0.0002576588303782046, -0.006034203805029392, -0.007746388204395771, -0.015386387705802917, 0.04335317760705948, -0.008557598106563091, 0.02164999023079872, 0.010226561687886715, -0.005658520385622978, 0.0024535770062357187, -0.004092619754374027, -0.010545726865530014, -0.01012682355940342, -0.0015833551296964288, 0.007620051968842745, -0.022381410002708435, -0.001702210633084178, -0.00645975628